[Term]
id: HP:0000005
name: Mode de transmission  {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Mode of inheritance", babelon:comment="label of HP:0000005 (Mode of inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Mode of inheritance
name: Modo de herencia {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Mode of inheritance", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
alt_id: HP:0001425
alt_id: HP:0001453
alt_id: HP:0001461
alt_id: HP:0010985
def: "Le mode de transmission, d'une génération à l'autre, d'un caractère ou d'une maladie génétique" [] {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="The pattern in which a particular genetic trait or disorder is passed from one generation to the next.", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:comment="definition of HP:0000005 (Mode of inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:source_language="en"}
def: "The pattern in which a particular genetic trait or disorder is passed from one generation to the next." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: [PROMOT note] [Derived from EURO-NMD NMD-CDE] [gendia_inher]
comment: [PROMOT note] [EURO-NMD] Atalia A et al., EURO-NMD registry: federated FAIR infrastructure, innovative technologies and concepts of a patient-centred registry for rare neuromuscular disorders. Orphanet J Rare Dis. 2024 Feb 14;19(1):66. doi: 10.1186/s13023-024-03059-3. PMID: 38355534; PMCID: PMC10865673.
comment: While there is a close conceptual relationship between allelic requirement and inheritance, they serve different purposes; allelic requirement is necessary for variant annotation pipelines and to determine if a given variant in a specific context is relevant to the phenotype of the patient e.g. a heterozygous variant (in the absence of compound heterozygosity) is relevant for dominant but not for recessive disease; while inheritance is used for describing the mode of inheritance of a phenotype and is particularly applicable in the clinical setting for communicating recurrence risk, to guide family screening, and to guide reproductive advice.
synonym: "Inheritance" EXACT []
synonym: "Mode d'héritage" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission" EXACT []
