[Term]
id: HP:0000006
name: Autosomal dominant inheritance
name: Herencia autosómica dominante {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Autosomal dominant inheritance", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Transmission autosomique dominante {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Autosomal dominant inheritance", babelon:comment="label of HP:0000006 (Autosomal dominant inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:source_language="en"}
alt_id: HP:0001415
alt_id: HP:0001447
alt_id: HP:0001448
alt_id: HP:0001451
alt_id: HP:0001452
alt_id: HP:0001455
alt_id: HP:0001456
alt_id: HP:0001463
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in heterozygotes. In the context of medical genetics, an autosomal dominant disorder is caused when a single copy of the mutant allele is present. Males and females are affected equally, and can both transmit the disorder with a risk of 50% for each child of inheriting the mutant allele." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
def: "Un mode de transmission qui concerne les caractères associés à un gène porté par un autosome (c.-à-d., les chromosomes 1 à 22 chez l'être humain), et où le caractère se manifeste chez les porteurs hétérozygotes. Dans le cadre de la génétique médicale, une maladie autosomique dominante survient lorsqu’une seule copie de l’allèle muté est présente. Les hommes et les femmes sont touchés de la même manière, et peuvent tous deux transmettre la maladie avec un risque de 50 % que chaque enfant hérite de l’allèle muté" [] {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="definition of HP:0000006 (Autosomal dominant inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:source_value="A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in heterozygotes. In the context of medical genetics, an autosomal dominant disorder is caused when a single copy of the mutant allele is present. Males and females are affected equally, and can both transmit the disorder with a risk of 50% for each child of inheriting the mutant allele."}
comment: [PROMOT note] [Derived from EURO-NMD NMD-CDE] [gendia_inher]
comment: [PROMOT note] [EURO-NMD] Atalia A et al., EURO-NMD registry: federated FAIR infrastructure, innovative technologies and concepts of a patient-centred registry for rare neuromuscular disorders. Orphanet J Rare Dis. 2024 Feb 14;19(1):66. doi: 10.1186/s13023-024-03059-3. PMID: 38355534; PMCID: PMC10865673.
synonym: "Autosomal dominant" EXACT []
synonym: "Autosomal dominant form" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autosomal dominant type" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Forme autosomique dominante" EXACT []
synonym: "monoallelic_autosomal" EXACT allelic_requirement []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante avec expression variable et pénétrance incomplète" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante avec pénétrance réduite" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission habituellement autosomique dominante" EXACT []
