[Term]
id: HP:0000007
name: Autosomal recessive inheritance
name: Herencia autosómica recesiva {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es", babelon:source_value="Autosomal recessive inheritance"}
name: Transmission autosomique récessive {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0000007 (Autosomal recessive inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:source_value="Autosomal recessive inheritance"}
alt_id: HP:0001416
alt_id: HP:0001526
alt_id: HP:0031362
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in individuals with two pathogenic alleles, either homozygotes (two copies of the same mutant allele) or compound heterozygotes (whereby each copy of a gene has a distinct mutant allele)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
def: "Un mode de transmission qui concerne les caractères associés à un gène porté par un autosome (c.-à-d., les chromosomes 1 à 22 chez l'être humain), et où le caractère se manifeste chez les porteurs homozygotes. Dans le cadre de la génétique médicale, une maladie autosomique récessive se manifeste chez les porteurs homozygotes (présence de deux allèles mutés identiques) ou chez les hétérozygotes composites (présence de deux allèles mutés différents)" [] {babelon:source_value="A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in individuals with two pathogenic alleles, either homozygotes (two copies of the same mutant allele) or compound heterozygotes (whereby each copy of a gene has a distinct mutant allele).", babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="definition of HP:0000007 (Autosomal recessive inheritance)  ; inheritance", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
comment: [PROMOT note] [Derived from EURO-NMD NMD-CDE] [gendia_inher]
