[Term]
id: HP:0000276
name: Cara larga {babelon:source_value="Long face", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Face longue {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0000276 (Long face)  ; abnormality of head or neck", babelon:source_value="Long face", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Long face
alt_id: HP:0000334
def: "Facial height (length) is more than 2 standard deviations above the mean (objective); or, an apparent increase in the height (length) of the face (subjective)." [PMID:19125436]
def: "La hauteur (longueur) du visage est supérieure à 2 écarts-types au-dessus de la moyenne (objective) ; ou, une augmentation apparente de la hauteur (longueur) du visage (subjective)." [] {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="definition of HP:0000276 (Long face)  ; abnormality of head or neck", babelon:source_value="Facial height (length) is more than 2 standard deviations above the mean (objective); or, an apparent increase in the height (length) of the face (subjective).", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
comment: Objective measurement of the face height is made with sliding calipers from the nasion, just above the depth of the nasal root, to the gnathion, the inferior border of the mandible, both in the midline. Note that long face is distinct from narrow face.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Elongation of face" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
