[Term]
id: HP:0000301
name: Abnormality of facial musculature
name: Anomalie de la musculature faciale {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="Abnormality of facial musculature", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:comment="label of HP:0000301 (Abnormality of facial musculature)  ; abnormality of the musculature ; abnormality of head or neck", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Anomalía de la musculatura facial {babelon:source_value="Abnormality of facial musculature", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
def: "An anomaly of a muscle that is innervated by the facial nerve (the seventh cranial nerve)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
def: "Anomalie d'un muscle innervé par le nerf facial (septième nerf crânien)" [] {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="definition of HP:0000301 (Abnormality of facial musculature)  ; abnormality of the musculature ; abnormality of head or neck", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="An anomaly of a muscle that is innervated by the facial nerve (the seventh cranial nerve).", babelon:source_language="en"}
comment: Facial muscles control facial expression and are innervated by the seventh cranial nerve. Facial muscles around the eye are responsible for eye blink and eyelid closure.
