[Term]
id: HP:0005216
name: Difficultés de mastication {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="Impaired mastication", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:comment="label of HP:0005216 (Impaired mastication)  ; abnormality of head or neck"}
name: Dificultad para la masticación {babelon:source_value="Impaired mastication", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Impaired mastication
def: "An abnormal reduction in the ability to masticate (chew), i.e., in the ability to crush and ground food in preparation for swallowing." [PMID:23713640]
comment: Chewing and swallowing are interrelated. The act of chewing plays a fundamental role in the process of swallowing food. Mastication prepares food for swallowing by breaking it into small particles. Accordingly, loss of teeth has been associated with swallowing difficulties. Chewing difficulties may be caused by loss of teeth, partial dentures, or by tooth pain. Swallowing difficulties, in contrast, are often characterized by difficulties swallowing liquids, reflux, throat spasms, choking on dry food, or dysphagia.
synonym: "Chewing difficulties" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Chewing difficulties|Chewing difficulty|Difficulty chewing" EXACT []
synonym: "Chewing difficulty" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Difficulty chewing" EXACT layperson []
