[Term]
id: HP:0012758
name: Neurodevelopmental delay
name: Retard de développement neurologique {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0012758 (Neurodevelopmental delay)  ; abnormality of the nervous system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Neurodevelopmental delay", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Retraso del desarrollo neurológico {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Neurodevelopmental delay", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
def: "Neurodevelopmental delay (NDD) refers to delays in the maturation of the brain and central nervous system; infants and young children with NDD may experience delays in the development of one or more skills including gross motor abilities, fine-motor coordination, language abilities and ability to solve increasingly complex problems." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157, PMID:31783983]
comment: Though the definitions of NDD vary broadly in the literature, all are used to signify a delay in one or more developmental domains compared to typical development.
synonym: "NDD" EXACT abbreviation []
xref: UMLS:C4022738
is_a: HP:0012759 ! Neurodevelopmental abnormality
property_value: dcterms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: dcterms:date "2014-04-03T12:16:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012759
name: Anomalie du développement neurologique {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0012759 (Neurodevelopmental abnormality)  ; abnormality of the nervous system", babelon:source_value="Neurodevelopmental abnormality", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Anomalía en el desarrollo neurológico {babelon:source_value="Neurodevelopmental abnormality", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Neurodevelopmental abnormality
def: "A deviation from normal of the neurological development of a child, which may include any or all of the aspects of the development of personal, social, gross or fine motor, and cognitive abilities." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:KI_phemming]
comment: This term should be used to describe abnormalities with onset in the developmental period.
xref: UMLS:C4022737
