[Term]
id: HP:0012823
name: Clinical modifier
name: Modificador clínico {babelon:source_value="Clinical modifier", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Modificateur clinique {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="Clinical modifier", babelon:comment="label of HP:0012823 (Clinical modifier)  ; modifier", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
alt_id: HP:0000004
def: "This subontology is designed to provide terms to characterize and specify the phenotypic abnormalities defined in the Phenotypic abnormality subontology, with respect to severity, laterality, age of onset, and other aspects." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: [PROMOT note] [Derived from EURO-NMD NMD-CDE] 
comment: [PROMOT note] [Derived from RD-CDM] [6.2.1 Phenotypic Feature] 
comment: [PROMOT note] [EURO-NMD] Atalia A et al., EURO-NMD registry: federated FAIR infrastructure, innovative technologies and concepts of a patient-centred registry for rare neuromuscular disorders. Orphanet J Rare Dis. 2024 Feb 14;19(1):66. doi: 10.1186/s13023-024-03059-3. PMID: 38355534; PMCID: PMC10865673.
comment: [PROMOT note] [RD-CDM] Graefe, A.S.L., Hübner, M.R., Rehburg, F. et al. An ontology-based rare disease common data model harmonising international registries, FHIR, and Phenopackets. Sci Data 12, 234 (2025). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04558-z
comment: Note that some of the terms, such as Intellectual disability, have children terms such as Severe intellectual disability that represent precomposed combinations of modifiers and phenotypic abnormality terms. This done where the medical community commonly uses these terms with a fixed meaning (for instance, the Intellectual disability terms are used with specific IQ ranges). For computational reasoning, the semantics are intended to be the same as if there was a combination of the phenotype term and the clinical modifier term.
synonym: "Phenotypic modifier" EXACT []
