[Term]
id: HP:0025031
name: Abnormality of the digestive system
name: Anomalie de l'appareil digestif {babelon:source_value="Abnormality of the digestive system", babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0025031 (Abnormality of the digestive system)  ; abnormality of the digestive system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Anomalía del sistema digestivo {babelon:source_value="Abnormality of the digestive system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
comment: Any anomaly of the digestive system, a collection of organs that is made up of the gastrointestinal tract and the liver, pancreas, and gallbladder. The gastrointestinal tract is a series of hollow organs joined in a long, twisting tube from the mouth to the anus, including the mouth, esophagus, stomach, small intestine, large intestine and anus.
