[Term]
id: HP:0025142
name: Constitutional symptom
name: Symptôme constitutionnel {babelon:comment="label of HP:0025142 (Constitutional symptom)  ; constitutional symptom", babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="Constitutional symptom", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
name: Síntoma constitucional {babelon:source_value="Constitutional symptom", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
def: "A symptom or manifestation indicating a systemic or general effect of a disease and that may affect the general well-being or status of an individual." []
comment: Note that we use the preferred term label constitutional symptom because this reflects common usage, but we do not restrict the term or its descendents to the narrow meaning of symptom, i.e., a complaint related by a patient to a physician. There is no generally accepted classification of what defines a constitutional symptom, but examples include weight loss, fatigue, general weakness, night sweats, shaking, chills, fever, and vomiting.
is_a: HP:0000118 ! Anomalía fenotípica
property_value: dcterms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: dcterms:date "2016-11-29T11:02:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025156
name: Dependencia de nutrición parenteral {babelon:source_value="Dependency on intravenous nutrition", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Dependency on intravenous nutrition
name: Dépendance à la nutrition intraveineuse {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:source_value="Dependency on intravenous nutrition", babelon:comment="label of HP:0025156 (Dependency on intravenous nutrition)  ; abnormality of the digestive system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en"}
def: "Inability to be weaned from intravenous (parenteral) nutrition, as judged by the hydration status (urine output, blood urea nitrogen, creatinine, urine sodium concentration), ability to maintain weight, stool output, and serum electrolyte status." [PMID:16770168]
comment: Total parenteral nutrition (TPN) refers to the application of an intravenous nutritional solution in individuals with gastrointestinal disorders that prevent them from absorbing a sufficient amount of nutrients from the gut to maintain health. The solution contains protein, carbohydrates (in the form of glucose), glucose, fat, vitamins, and minerals. Dependency on TPN is essentially a manifestation of the continued severity of a gastrointestinal disorder.
synonym: "Dependency on IV nutrition" EXACT abbreviation []
