[Term]
id: HP:0025766
name: Abnormal affect
name: Afecto anormal {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Abnormal affect", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
def: "An anomaly in intensity, frequency, or duration of the verbal or behavioral expression of emotions, feelings, or thoughts." [PMID:37925091]
comment: Affect includes a combination of emotion in terms of feelings and its expression either in the verbal or behavioral (action) level. Normal expressions are often relatively short lived and familiar to the person while pathological expressions may be intense and extended and considered out of character for the individual. Affect encompasses: 1) emotions, 2) volition, and 3) what is termed the intellect or cognitive elements expressing (communicating) emotion and volition. Affect includes an internal feeling (emotion), an internal drive (will), and a motor component expression (typically speech, but also reflected in thoughts).
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Anomalie des fonctions mentales supérieures
property_value: dcterms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: dcterms:date "2024-07-21T12:00:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025792
name: Abnormal cognitive process
name: Proceso cognitivo anormal {babelon:source_value="Abnormal cognitive process", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
def: "An abnormal cognitive process can be defined as a deviation from the typical development, structural organization, or functional execution of mental operations that connect informational inputs to behavioral outputs, typically involve at least one of the following processes: perception, memory, learning, emotion, intentionality, self-representation, rationality, and decision-making." []
comment: Definition adapted from Newen A (2017) What are cognitive processes? An example-based approach. Synthese 194:4251-4268.
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Anomalie des fonctions mentales supérieures
property_value: dcterms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: dcterms:date "2024-08-07T17:25:08Z" xsd:dateTime

