[Term]
id: HP:0030201
name: Response to drugs acting on neuromuscular transmission
name: Respuesta a medicamentos que actúan sobre la transmisión neuromuscular {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Response to drugs acting on neuromuscular transmission", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Réponse aux médicaments agissant sur la transmission neuromusculaire {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:comment="label of HP:0030201 (Response to drugs acting on neuromuscular transmission)  ; abnormality of the nervous system", babelon:source_value="Response to drugs acting on neuromuscular transmission", babelon:source_language="en"}
def: "Specific drugs interfere selectively with the different cellular mechanisms involved in neuromuscular transmission (synthesis, storage, release, action and inactivation of transmitter). The response of a patient to a specific drug can therefore be useful information for the differential diagnosis." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UK_rheller]
xref: UMLS:C4022582
is_a: HP:0030191 ! Transmission synaptique anormale du système nerveux périphérique

[Term]
id: HP:0030202
name: Favorable response of weakness to acetylcholine esterase inhibitors
name: Respuesta favorable a la debilidad muscular de los inhibidores de la acetilcolinesterasa {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Favorable response of weakness to acetylcholine esterase inhibitors", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Réponse favorable de la faiblesse aux inhibiteurs de l'acétylcholine estérase {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0030202 (Favorable response of weakness to acetylcholine esterase inhibitors)  ; abnormality of the nervous system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Favorable response of weakness to acetylcholine esterase inhibitors", babelon:source_language="en"}
def: "Improvement of muscle strength in response to administration of an acetylcholine esterase inhibitor." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UK_rheller]
comment: An acetylcholinesterase inhibitor inhibits acetylcholinesterase from breaking down acetylcholine, thereby increasing both the level and duration of action of the neurotransmitter acetylcholine. For instance, edrophonium is a readily reversible acetylcholinesterase inhibitor that can be used to differentiate myasthenia gravis from cholinergic crisis. Edrophonium would improve muscle weakness in myasthenia gravis but not in cholinergic crisis.
synonym: "Favourable response of weakness to acetylcholine esterase inhibitors" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: UMLS:C4022581
is_a: HP:0030201 ! Response to drugs acting on neuromuscular transmission
relationship: PROMOT:2000005 SNOMED:84100007 ! est évalué par History taking
