id: HP:0030884
name: Alimentación por sonda gastroyeyunal en la infancia {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:source_value="Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Alimentation par sonde gastro-jéjunale dans la petite enfance {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0030884 (Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy)  ; abnormality of the digestive system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:source_value="Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy"}
name: Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy
def: "Feeding problem necessitating gastrojejunal tube feeding." [PMID:11827911]
comment: The rationale for gastrojejunal tube feeding is that placing the tip of the tube beyond the ligament of Treitz prevented duodenogastric reflux or gastro-esophageal reflux. Gastrojejunal feeding tubes have since been used in children who are deemed too unfit for antireflux surgery or where fundoplication has failed.
synonym: "Gastro-jejunal tube feeding in infancy" EXACT []
