[Term]
id: HP:0100261
name: Abnormal tendon morphology
name: Morfología del tendón anormal {babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Abnormal tendon morphology", babelon:source_language="en", babelon:translation_language="es"}
name: Morphologie anormale des tendons {babelon:translation_language="fr", babelon:comment="label of HP:0100261 (Abnormal tendon morphology)  ; abnormality of the skeletal system", babelon:translation_status="OFFICIAL", babelon:source_value="Abnormal tendon morphology", babelon:source_language="en"}
def: "An abnormality of the structure or form of the tendons, also often called sinews." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
comment: A tendon (or sinew) is a tough band of fibrous connective tissue that usually connects muscle to bone and is capable of withstanding tension. Tendons are similar to ligaments and fascia as they are all made of collagen except that ligaments join one bone to another bone, and fascia connect muscles to other muscles. Tendons and muscles work together and can only exert a pulling force.
synonym: "Abnormal shape of tendon" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Abnormal shape of tendon|Abnormality of the sinew" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of the sinew" EXACT []
